{
  "information": {
    "title": "ℹ About FLUVI",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "FLUVI"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Vehicular Flow Management System Simulator for Roads Near Academic Areas of IPN - ESCOM"
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "1 Introduction"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "FLUVI is a vehicular traffic simulator based on cellular automata designed specifically to analyze and optimize vehicle flow on roads near academic areas of the Instituto Politécnico Nacional, focusing on the Escuela Superior de Cómputo (ESCOM)."
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "The system can model complex urban traffic scenarios, including:"
      },
      {
        "kind": "item",
        "text": "Multiple interconnected lanes and streets"
      },
      {
        "kind": "item",
        "text": "Dynamic vehicle generation"
      },
      {
        "kind": "item",
        "text": "Lane changes with configurable probabilities"
      },
      {
        "kind": "item",
        "text": "Intersection detection and resolution"
      },
      {
        "kind": "item",
        "text": "Real-time visualization of traffic metrics"
      },
      {
        "kind": "item",
        "text": "Streets with customizable curves"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "This project arises from the need to understand and improve vehicular circulation in academic areas, allowing researchers and urban planners to simulate different scenarios before implementing changes to real infrastructure."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "2 Algorithms"
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "Rule 184 of Cellular Automata"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "FLUVI implements a modified version of Rule 184, a one-dimensional cellular automaton that efficiently simulates traffic flow."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "What is Rule 184?"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Rule 184 is a cellular automaton that models vehicular traffic where each cell can be empty (0) or occupied by a vehicle (1). Vehicles move forward if the next cell is empty, creating a natural traffic flow."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "Basic Operation of Rule 184"
      },
      {
        "kind": "row",
        "text": "Left  |  Center  |  Right  |  →  |  New State (Center)"
      },
      {
        "kind": "row",
        "text": "1  |  1  |  1  |  →  |  1"
      },
      {
        "kind": "row",
        "text": "1  |  1  |  0  |  →  |  0"
      },
      {
        "kind": "row",
        "text": "1  |  0  |  1  |  →  |  1"
      },
      {
        "kind": "row",
        "text": "1  |  0  |  0  |  →  |  0"
      },
      {
        "kind": "row",
        "text": "0  |  1  |  1  |  →  |  1"
      },
      {
        "kind": "row",
        "text": "0  |  1  |  0  |  →  |  1"
      },
      {
        "kind": "row",
        "text": "0  |  0  |  1  |  →  |  0"
      },
      {
        "kind": "row",
        "text": "0  |  0  |  0  |  →  |  0"
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "Modifications Implemented in FLUVI"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "We have adapted and extended the classic Rule 184 to support more complex and realistic traffic scenarios:"
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "1 Multi-lane"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "We expand the one-dimensional rule to a system of multiple lanes, allowing vehicles to change lanes based on configurable probabilities."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "2 Waiting Cells"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "We introduce the concept of waiting cells to handle temporary blockages (such as intersections or congested connections), preventing collisions."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "3 Street Connections"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "We implement three types of connections: linear (1-to-1), incorporation (N-to-1) and probabilistic (1-to-N with distribution)."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "4 Intersection Resolution"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "We add an alternating priority system to resolve conflicts at intersections, simulating traffic lights or right-of-way rules."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "5 X-Crossing Prevention"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "We implement logic to prevent crossed lane changes (X pattern) where two adjacent vehicles attempt to swap lanes simultaneously."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "6 Curved Streets"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "We extend the model to non-linear geometries through a vertex system with angular interpolation for streets with curves."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "Result"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "These modifications make it possible to simulate complex urban traffic scenarios while maintaining the computational efficiency of cellular automata, with real-time updates and support for thousands of simultaneous vehicles."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "3 File Format"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "FLUVI uses JSON format to save and load complete simulations."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "JSON file structure:"
      },
      {
        "kind": "code",
        "text": "{\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"nombre\": \"Nombre de la Simulación\",\n  \"fecha\": \"2024-01-01T12:00:00.000Z\",\n  \"calles\": [\n    {\n      \"nombre\": \"Calle Principal\",\n      \"tamano\": 100,\n      \"tipo\": \"CONEXION\",\n      \"carriles\": 3,\n      \"x\": 500,\n      \"y\": 300,\n      \"angulo\": 0,\n      \"probabilidadGeneracion\": 0.5,\n      \"probabilidadSaltoDeCarril\": 0.02,\n      \"esCurva\": false,\n      \"vertices\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"conexiones\": [\n    {\n      \"tipo\": \"LINEAL\",\n      \"origen\": \"Calle1\",\n      \"destino\": \"Calle2\",\n      \"carrilOrigen\": 0,\n      \"carrilDestino\": 0\n    }\n  ],\n  \"edificios\": [\n    {\n      \"label\": \"ESCOM\",\n      \"x\": 1000,\n      \"y\": 500,\n      \"width\": 200,\n      \"height\": 150\n    }\n  ]\n}"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Tip: You can export your current simulation using the \"Save Simulation\" button in the Map Constructor."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "text": "4 Warnings"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Some known issues and current limitations of the system:"
      },
      {
        "kind": "item",
        "text": "Performance in very large simulations: Simulations with more than 50 long streets may experience FPS drops."
      },
      {
        "kind": "item",
        "text": "Collisions on very sharp curves: Extreme curvatures (±40°) can occasionally produce visual overlaps."
      },
      {
        "kind": "item",
        "text": "Compatibility with older browsers: Requires ES6+ and Canvas API support."
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Note: We are continuously working on improvements and fixes. If you find any problem, please report it to the development team."
      },
      {
